%U A376235 1237,1279,1303,1307,1319,1381,1427,1429,1433,1471,1481,1489,1531,1559,1579,1607,1613,1619,1621,1637,1663
%N A376235 Prime numbers with Hamming weight neither prime nor a power of 2.
%C A376235 Surprisingly, all primes less than 311 have a Hamming weight (sum of their binary digits: A000120) equal to either a prime or a power of two (cf. A174090). But for larger primes, exceptions become more and more frequent.
%H A376235 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A376235/b376235.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%t A376235 q[p_] := Module[{h = DigitSum[p, 2]}, !PrimeQ[h] && h != 2^IntegerExponent[h, 2]]; Select[Prime[Range[261]], q] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 17 2026 *)
%o A376235 (PARI) select( {is_A376235(n)=!is_A174090(hammingweight(n))&&isprime(n)}, [0..2222])
%Y A376235 Cf. A000120 (binary or Hamming weight), A174090 (union of primes and powers of two).
%K A376235 nonn,changed
%O A376235 1,1
%A A376235 _M. F. Hasler_, Oct 24 2024
